WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.799 --> 00:00:06.350
In this lesson, we build acrylic extensions on forms, step by step.

00:00:06.931 --> 00:00:08.830
Keep in mind three things throughout:

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.435
the bead at the right moisture, no acrylic on the skin,

00:00:12.385 --> 00:00:14.270
and the apex in the right place.

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:15.711
Step one:

00:00:15.964 --> 00:00:17.551
consultation and check.

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:21.391
Wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client.

00:00:21.803 --> 00:00:24.431
Look closely at the nails and the skin around them.

00:00:24.786 --> 00:00:30.196
If a nail is separating from the bed or discolored, or the skin is red, swollen,

00:00:30.146 --> 00:00:31.871
has pus or an open wound,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.791
do not do the service, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.494
Ask whether the client has ever had itching,

00:00:38.444 --> 00:00:40.911
redness or blistering after a nail service.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.631
Ask how long she wants them, and what shape.

00:00:44.058 --> 00:00:45.071
And tell her up front:

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:48.431
she should come back for an infill in about two to three weeks.

00:00:48.777 --> 00:00:51.631
Before you start, switch on the extraction at the table.

00:00:52.287 --> 00:00:53.072
Step two:

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.552
dry prep, as in the gel polish lesson.

00:00:55.727 --> 00:00:56.512
No soaking.

00:00:57.027 --> 00:00:58.631
Push back the cuticle gently,

00:00:58.581 --> 00:01:01.952
removing the thin layer of skin still stuck to the nail plate.

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.432
File the free edge short and neat.

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:09.312
Buff lightly to remove the shine, brush off the dust, then cleanse the nails.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.352
From now on, do not touch the nail surface.

00:01:12.911 --> 00:01:13.715
Step three:

00:01:13.972 --> 00:01:18.275
dehydrator and primer, the right type, applied the way the brand instructs.

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:21.795
Just one very thin layer, on the nail plate only.

00:01:22.144 --> 00:01:24.755
Keep well away from the skin and the side corners.

00:01:25.025 --> 00:01:27.475
Then let it dry, for the time the brand gives.

00:01:28.145 --> 00:01:28.924
Step four:

00:01:29.108 --> 00:01:30.044
fit the form.

00:01:30.564 --> 00:01:34.684
The form must sit right under the free edge, snug, with no gap.

00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:38.124
Seen from above, the form lines up with the finger.

00:01:38.451 --> 00:01:43.177
Seen from the side, the form continues the line of the nail, not pointing down,

00:01:43.127 --> 00:01:44.124
not pointing up.

00:01:44.472 --> 00:01:49.484
If there is a gap, the acrylic runs underneath, and the nail is both ugly and weak.

00:01:49.722 --> 00:01:54.877
If you use tips, glue a tip that fits the width of the nail exactly, cut it short,

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:57.804
and file the seam thin before applying acrylic.

00:01:58.439 --> 00:01:59.338
Step five:

00:01:59.511 --> 00:02:00.538
set up your table.

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:04.938
Pour a little liquid into a small covered dish, just enough for one client.

00:02:05.331 --> 00:02:06.457
Open the powder jar.

00:02:06.884 --> 00:02:09.607
Dip the brush into the liquid so it soaks in evenly,

00:02:09.557 --> 00:02:12.538
then wipe the brush lightly against the edge of the dish,

00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:13.738
to remove the excess.

00:02:14.163 --> 00:02:18.538
How much liquid is in the brush is exactly what decides whether the bead is wet or dry.

00:02:19.202 --> 00:02:20.059
Step six:

00:02:20.304 --> 00:02:21.179
pick up the bead.

00:02:21.715 --> 00:02:24.731
Touch the tip of the brush to the surface of the powder,

00:02:24.681 --> 00:02:26.373
and hold it still for a moment,

00:02:26.323 --> 00:02:29.499
so the liquid soaks into the powder and forms a round bead.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.019
Then lift the brush.

00:02:31.411 --> 00:02:32.299
Look at the bead:

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:37.819
moist, glossy, round, not dripping, and not dry and crumbly.

00:02:38.236 --> 00:02:41.579
At first, small beads are easier to control than big ones.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.105
Step seven:

00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:46.209
the first bead goes at the tip, on the form,

00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:48.865
just in front of the edge of the natural nail.

00:02:49.359 --> 00:02:54.274
Wait a moment for the bead to spread, then lay the belly of the brush almost flat,

00:02:54.224 --> 00:02:55.105
press lightly,

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.265
and stroke it into the extended tip.

00:02:57.745 --> 00:03:01.585
Keep the side walls straight, continuing the sides of the natural nail.

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:04.705
The length and the tip shape are created with this bead.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:09.265
Between beads, wipe the brush on a paper towel, and dip it in liquid again.

00:03:09.927 --> 00:03:10.720
Step eight:

00:03:11.028 --> 00:03:14.522
the second bead goes in the middle of the nail, on the stress area,

00:03:14.472 --> 00:03:16.320
where the nail leaves the skin bed.

00:03:16.646 --> 00:03:18.640
This is the bead that builds the apex.

00:03:18.899 --> 00:03:22.270
Press lightly, stroke it so it joins smoothly with the tip,

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.240
and spread it evenly to both sides.

00:03:24.907 --> 00:03:25.774
Step nine:

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.214
the third bead, smaller, goes near the cuticle.

00:03:29.544 --> 00:03:33.541
Stroke it very thin, thinner and thinner towards the skin,

00:03:33.491 --> 00:03:35.854
and leave a gap as thin as a hair.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.414
The acrylic must never touch the skin.

00:03:38.804 --> 00:03:43.496
If it does, flick it away right away with the tip of the brush or a wooden stick,

00:03:43.446 --> 00:03:44.814
while it is still soft.

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:49.457
Finally, stroke lightly over the whole surface so it is seamless and smooth,

00:03:49.407 --> 00:03:51.054
from the cuticle to the tip.

00:03:51.717 --> 00:03:52.502
Step ten:

00:03:52.881 --> 00:03:54.422
wait for the acrylic to harden.

00:03:55.007 --> 00:03:58.022
The time depends on the brand, usually just a few minutes.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:00.662
Tap the brush handle lightly on the nail:

00:04:00.918 --> 00:04:04.342
when you hear a dry, clear click, the acrylic has hardened.

00:04:04.772 --> 00:04:09.062
Do not take off the form while the acrylic is still soft, or the tip will warp.

00:04:09.495 --> 00:04:14.342
Then remove the form gently, pulling it downwards, not bending it backwards and up.

00:04:14.957 --> 00:04:16.263
Check before you file.

00:04:16.513 --> 00:04:17.543
From the side:

00:04:17.585 --> 00:04:22.423
thin at the cuticle, highest over the stress area, then thinner towards the tip.

00:04:22.764 --> 00:04:23.543
From the tip:

00:04:23.854 --> 00:04:26.263
the C curve is even on both sides.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.143
From above:

00:04:27.403 --> 00:04:30.183
the side walls are straight, and the tip is balanced.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.621
Step eleven:

00:04:31.882 --> 00:04:32.581
filing.

00:04:32.954 --> 00:04:35.381
With the extraction running, put on a mask.

00:04:35.648 --> 00:04:37.061
File with a light hand.

00:04:37.329 --> 00:04:40.981
Press hard, and the nail heats up, and the client will feel burning.

00:04:41.492 --> 00:04:43.381
File the tip into the right shape.

00:04:43.743 --> 00:04:45.381
File the side walls straight.

00:04:45.804 --> 00:04:49.301
Then file the surface smooth and even, keeping the apex.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.878
At the cuticle, file it really thin, so it blends in smoothly,

00:04:53.828 --> 00:04:56.341
but do not file into the natural nail.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:05:01.861
Glide a fine buffer over it, brush off the dust, do not blow, then cleanse.

00:05:02.438 --> 00:05:03.393
Step twelve:

00:05:03.625 --> 00:05:04.913
color and finish.

00:05:05.487 --> 00:05:09.393
If the client likes a natural look, one glossy top coat is enough.

00:05:09.726 --> 00:05:15.073
If she wants color, paint it on top, thin and even, as in the gel polish lesson.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:19.633
Then put a drop of cuticle oil around the nails, and massage gently.

00:05:20.251 --> 00:05:21.161
Tell the client:

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.921
do not pick at them, and do not use your nails as tools.

00:05:25.306 --> 00:05:27.641
Wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:05:27.989 --> 00:05:29.321
Use oil every day.

00:05:29.654 --> 00:05:31.961
If something lifts, come back to the salon;

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.281
do not glue it or peel it yourself.

00:05:34.548 --> 00:05:37.961
And book the infill right away, for about two to three weeks later.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.798
At the end of the day:

00:05:39.916 --> 00:05:43.942
clean the brush with the liquid of the brand itself, not with acetone,

00:05:43.892 --> 00:05:46.838
because acetone dries out and damages the bristles.

00:05:47.226 --> 00:05:51.076
Wipe the brush, shape it back to a point, and store it lying flat,

00:05:51.026 --> 00:05:52.918
or the way the brand recommends.

00:05:53.342 --> 00:05:55.398
Close the dish and the bottle tightly.

00:05:55.745 --> 00:05:58.038
Leftover liquid does not go down the sink;

00:05:58.307 --> 00:06:01.238
dispose of it according to the safety data sheet of the product.

00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:05.798
Disposables go in a bin with a lid, and metal tools go to be sterilized.

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:08.678
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
